meta {
  name: Get Carrier Appointments
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/agency/carrier-appointments
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{appointmentsOwnerToken}}
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.getStatus() === 200) {
    const allstate = res.getBody().carrierOptions.find((c) => c.name === "Allstate");
    if (allstate) bru.setVar("appointmentCarrierId", allstate.id);
    const other = res.getBody().carrierOptions.find((c) => c.name !== "Allstate");
    if (other) bru.setVar("appointmentOtherCarrierId", other.id);
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("carries the pickable carriers alongside the appointments", function () {
    // The options ride along so the settings page never has to call the
    // module-gated `GET /carriers` — see the docs block.
    expect(res.getBody().appointments).to.be.an("array");
    expect(res.getBody().carrierOptions.length).to.be.greaterThan(0);
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /agency/carrier-appointments — this agency's carrier codes

  Which carriers appointed this agency, and under what code (PAC-93). Backs
  Workspace Settings → Carrier Appointments and the owner's first-run setup
  step.

  - **Module:** none (`@SkipModule()`) — an appointment is agency identity, not
    a product module that can be switched off.
  - **Permission:** `agency:carrier_appointments:read`
  - **Data scope:** none — an appointment belongs to the agency, not to one of
    its branches, so `@SkipBranch()` is set.

  ## Why `carrierOptions` is in the response

  The obvious alternative — have the page call `GET /carriers` — breaks for an
  agency with neither `deal_audits` nor `crm_service` enabled, because that
  route is module-gated: their settings page would render a picker that 403s.
  Returning the options here also guarantees the picker offers exactly the set
  the `PUT` validates against (globals only).

  ## Response `200`
  ```json
  {
    "appointments": [
      { "carrierId": "6a86…", "carrierName": "Allstate",
        "carrierAgencyCode": "A0B9049", "isPrimary": true,
        "active": true, "appointedAt": null }
    ],
    "carrierOptions": [ { "id": "6a86…", "name": "Allstate",
                          "policyNumberPattern": "\\d+",
                          "policyNumberHint": null } ]
  }
  ```

  `carrierName` is resolved server-side, so no client has to join — and a
  carrier since deactivated in the catalog still renders.

  ## Errors
  - `401 Unauthorized` — missing/expired token.
  - `403 Forbidden` — the caller lacks `agency:carrier_appointments:read`. A
    producer gets this; so does a platform operator, who has no agency of their
    own.
}
